fyFuture.vote -> leaderLoop completion\"\n      ],\n      \"activity_classes\": [\n        \"A2\"\n      ],\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-verify-start\",\n        \"B-verify-support\",\n        \"B-verify-result\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-verify-tally\"\n      ],\n      \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n        \"B-config\": \"Defines distinct Voter and Nonvoter membership and creates replication state for both.\",\n        \"B-authority\": \"Separate voter-only lease check can later revoke authority; timing and scope must remain counterevidence.\"\n      },\n      \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"Commitment and leader lease do filter support to voters. A later lease check can step the leader down.\",\n        \"VerifyLeader may validly succeed before the leader has actually lost authority; missing current responses alone does not prove stale data or an elected successor.\",\n        \"Per-peer notification clearing and per-future completion suppression limit repeat counting; the selected issue is eligibility, not duplicate responses.\"\n      ],\n      \"unknowns\": [\n        \"Ground whether the local verification quorum must consist of voters from interface semantics and implementation use, rather than assuming every successful call witnesses a fresh election.\",\n        \"Construct a legal mixed-membership verification interval with isolated nonvoter support and no hidden eligible replies; compare completion without fabricating transport responses.\",\n        \"Distinguish local support eligibility failure from whole-cluster stale-read consequence and independent lease timing.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"trigger_rationale\": \"verifyLeader derives quorumSize from voter count but registers all replState entries; notifyAll forwards unqualified booleans and leaderLoop accepts numeric threshold. This direct producer/consumer discrepancy is more discriminating than testing already-explicit commitment filters or assuming storage error semantics.\"\n    },\n    \"status\": \"active\",\n    \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n    \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n    \"stop_reason\": \"Complete the sourced core overview and select the newly observed verification support-eligibility discrepancy; defer a formal requirement until its local contract and legal driver are fixed.\",\n    \"resume_conditions\": [],\n    \"obligation_id\": null,\n    \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n    \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n    \"executions\": [],\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"402cdfaeb47d4f148d7d6ab0184b7a23\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\ncapacity {\n  \"remaining\": {\n    \"agent_calls\": 37,\n    \"experiments\": 8,\n    \"audit_units\": 4,\n    \"semantic_reviews\": 6,\n    \"revisions\": 4\n  },\n  \"remaining_seconds\": 1382.821003178,\n  \"new_obligation\": true,\n  \"direct_execution\": true,\n  \"source_investigation\": true,\n  \"exhausted\": []\n}\nnext_objective {\n  \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n  \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n  \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n  \"core_gaps\": []\n}\npending_work [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"402cdfaeb47d4f148d7d6ab0184b7a23\",\n    \"kind\": \"candidate\",\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"402cdfaeb47d4f148d7d6ab0184b7a23\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Sources\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"repair_of\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"const\": \"explore\",\n      \"title\": \"Action\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"question\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Question\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"harness_path\": {\n      \"title\": \"Harness Path\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"execution_package\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Optional single local Go package or Rust crate directory, with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package\",\n      \"title\": \"Execution Package\"\n    },\n    \"files\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"title\": \"Files\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"action\",\n    \"question\",\n    \"harness_path\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ExploreSubmission\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n// Copyright (c) HashiCorp, Inc.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0\n\npackage raft\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"reflect\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/hashicorp/go-hclog\"\n\t\"github.com/hashicorp/go-msgpack/v2/codec\"\n)\n\nvar userSnapshotErrorsOnNoData = true\n\n// Return configurations optimized for in-memory\nfunc inmemConfig(t testing.TB) *Config {\n\tconf := DefaultConfig()\n\tconf.HeartbeatTimeout = 50 * time.Millisecond\n\tconf.ElectionTimeout = 50 * time.Millisecond\n\tconf.LeaderLeaseTimeout = 50 * time.Millisecond\n\tconf.CommitTimeout = 5 * time.Millisecond\n\tconf.Logger = newTestLogger(t)\n\treturn conf\n}\n\n// MockFSM is an implementation of the FSM interface, and just stores\n// the logs sequentially.\n//\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\ntype MockFSM struct {\n\tsync.Mutex\n\tlogs           [][]byte\n\tconfigurations []Configuration\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\ntype MockFSMConfigStore struct {\n\tFSM\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\ntype WrappingFSM interface {\n\tUnderlying() FSM\n}\n\nfunc getMockFSM(fsm FSM) *MockFSM {\n\tswitch f := fsm.(type) {\n\tcase *MockFSM:\n\t\treturn f\n\tcase *MockFSMConfigStore:\n\t\treturn f.FSM.(*MockFSM)\n\tcase WrappingFSM:\n\t\treturn getMockFSM(f.Underlying())\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\ntype MockSnapshot struct {\n\tlogs     [][]byte\n\tmaxIndex int\n}\n\nvar _ ConfigurationStore = (*MockFSMConfigStore)(nil)\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockFSM) Apply(log *Log) interface{} {\n\tm.Lock()\n\tdefer m.Unlock()\n\tm.logs = append(m.logs, log.Data)\n\treturn len(m.logs)\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockFSM) Snapshot() (FSMSnapshot, error) {\n\tm.Lock()\n\tdefer m.Unlock()\n\treturn &MockSnapshot{m.logs, len(m.logs)}, nil\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockFSM) Restore(inp io.ReadCloser) error {\n\tm.Lock()\n\tdefer m.Unlock()\n\tdefer inp.Close()\n\thd := codec.MsgpackHandle{}\n\tdec := codec.NewDecoder(inp, &hd)\n\n\tm.logs = nil\n\treturn dec.Decode(&m.logs)\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockFSM) Logs() [][]byte {\n\tm.Lock()\n\tdefer m.Unlock()\n\treturn m.logs\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockFSMConfigStore) StoreConfiguration(index uint64, config Configuration) {\n\tmm := m.FSM.(*MockFSM)\n\tmm.Lock()\n\tdefer mm.Unlock()\n\tmm.configurations = append(mm.configurations, config)\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockSnapshot) Persist(sink SnapshotSink) error {\n\thd := codec.MsgpackHandle{}\n\tenc := codec.NewEncoder(sink, &hd)\n\tif err := enc.Encode(m.logs[:m.maxIndex]); err != nil {\n\t\tsink.Cancel()\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tsink.Close()\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// NOTE: This is exposed for middleware testing purposes and is not a stable API\nfunc (m *MockSnapshot) Release() {\n}\n\n// MockMonotonicLogStore is a LogStore wrapper for testing the\n// MonotonicLogStore interface.\ntype MockMonotonicLogStore struct {\n\ts LogStore\n}\n\n// IsMonotonic implements the MonotonicLogStore interface.\nfunc (m *MockMonotonicLogStore) IsMonotonic() bool {\n\treturn true\n}\n\n// FirstIndex implements the LogStore interface.\nfunc (m *MockMonotonicLogStore) FirstIndex() (uint64, error) {\n\treturn m.s.FirstIndex()\n}\n\n// LastIndex implements the LogStore interface.\nfunc (m *MockMonotonicLogStore) LastIndex() (uint64, error) {\n\treturn m.s.LastIndex()\n}\n\n// GetLog implements the LogStore interface.\nfunc (m *MockMonotonicLogStore) GetLog(index uint64, log *Log) error {\n\treturn m.s.GetLog(index, log)\n}\n\n// StoreLog implements the LogStore interface.\nfunc (m *MockMonotonicLogStore) StoreLog(log *Log) error {\nEXECUTION Observe actual implementation effects under explicit inputs, caller policy and authorized isolation. Contract applicability may remain unresolved during exploration; execution permission may not. A changed value or tests_passed is not a violation oracle. Exploration remains construction knowledge: a later requirement needs a separately fixed check, fresh execution and correspondence review, not retroactive relabelling. Missing capability, compilation failure, timeout, panic and a completed property comparison remain distinct. Retain failures; never precompute expected observations or alter protocol behavior to create a finding.\n\nCOMPLETION Separate the proposition's observation endpoint, necessary caller completion, and resource cleanup. A normal nonzero test exit may leave a completed violating witness intact only through checker_correspondence.execution_attribution binding the exact target CheckRun, checker and valid event indices, retained failure stream lines and fixed harness lines. Use source_ids and rationale to justify that all duties needed by that witness completed before an independent failure, with no corruption of history, identity or values. Machine validation checks these references and eligibility, not causal independence; stdout/stderr line numbers are not a common clock. Ordinary no_issue_found never authorizes nonzero exits. Preserve raw failure, other scenario debts and later challenges; no holds-only, timeout, cancellation, signal, build failure, missing premise, ambiguous or contradictory observation can use this path. Do not remove required join/close, ignore exceptions or kill workers after printing to manufacture PASS; unsupported short wall-clock limits are not extra properties. Changed harnesses, premises, predicates or scope still need the existing new-artifact and actual-execution path. Initialization, driver compliance and observation validity belong in prerequisites, controls or diagnostics, not duplicate properties. Check a wait's return or record actual attainment when it establishes a necessary premise; when waiting is the investigated behavior, requiring success would discard the failure history. Sleep establishes elapsed time, not synchronization, completion or a coherent snapshot; a printed readiness flag is not a prerequisite witness. A diagnostic control need not satisfy the principal scenario's premises or acquire a separate obligation: select formal applicability from independently declared input/policy fields before execution, retaining control output. Distinct formal scenarios need their actual admission and premises; incompatible histories may need separate checks. Never select scenarios by observed results or missing premises after execution. Role readiness does not imply that earlier work drained. Across preparation, policy changes and delivery, preserve caller/transport duties; prefer one policy-selected delivery path and record the identity, provenance and order needed for attribution. Distinguish receipt, per-message-type queueing and dispatch; preserve the replaced layer's ordering without assuming global FIFO or arbitrary reordering. Legal in-flight work need not be emptied. End controlled work independently of the forbidden behavior. Observe admission, completion and final state for the same operation before treating absence as bounded holds. Missing completion, identity, result events and tool timeout remain unknown. A finite window records non-completion, not a deadline violation or infinite stalling. A repeatable suffix must account for behavior-determining state, schedule, queues, timers and callbacks; equal business fields do not close execution. A rescue stimulus may itself be required caller work.\n\nCORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias selects the declared prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is owed, not the first array entry. Harness.prerequisites contains prerequisites only; monitors select independent results. During construction, compare ObservableProperty.identity_fields with the actual prerequisite and result events together. Shared setup may support multiple operations through explicit plan relationships; neither duplicate identical events mechanic